AB  - Key objectives: To address the social determinants of health domains "social and community context" and "neighborhood and built environment" via Medically Tailored Meals; a nutrition intervention that includes home delivery; medical nutrition therapy and education; and frozen medically tailored meals provided by the non-profit partner. This intervention targeted Medicaid members exhibiting high healthcare utilization in conjunction with each individual's risk of developing higher morbidity and mortality of existing disease due to co-existing food and nutrition insecurity. The populations served include people living with Type 2 Diabetes; Hypertension; Cardiovascular Disease; Cancer; HIV/AIDS; and End-Stage Renal Disease; among other conditions; whose burden is disproportionately felt by people of color. Methodology: In this partnership; MetroPlus Health and God's Love We Deliver; Inc executed a service contract and business associate agreement. Through this contract; the organizations are jointly serving members and clients through three innovative healthcare pathways. To date; the partnership model has facilitated service provision for members as follows: 2210 members through Value-Based-Payment (VBP); 1599 members through In-Lieu-of Service (ILS); and 838 through our latest Discharge Meals (DM) collaboration; with an even greater number of referrals. The collaborative model includes monthly strategic calls; weekly key performance indicator (KPI) reports of enrollment metrics; daily referrals using a HIPAA-compliant interface; and compliant billing by the community-based organization. Enrollment and improvement metrics from this partnership provided support for the New York City (NYC) ILS pilot that is now an established program. This partnership; which is constantly evolving; will continue to adapt and grow with the approval and expected implementation of the New York State 1115 waiver. Expected contributions: Payer; Community-Based; and Clinical Partnerships framework.
